; ANSWER_DIVERGES_BY_VANTAGE_POINT, as far as it can be reproduced locally.
;
; Real GeoDNS and anycast are not reproducible on one host. Divergent *answers*
; are, and divergent answers are what the consensus logic actually consumes:
; query dns-auth and dns-divergent for the same name and get different results.
;
; This exists to test the property the README calls non-negotiable — that one
; disagreeing vantage point must produce `degraded`, never `failed`. Without a
; fixture, the hysteresis logic would be the least-tested and highest-stakes
; code in the product.
;
; The counterpart records live on dns-auth (zones/unsigned/divergent-peer.test.zone
; is not used; the peer name here is wildcard.test's _propgate-verify). Keep the
; two in step when either changes.
$ORIGIN divergent.test.
$TTL 60

@       IN SOA  ns-divergent.test. hostmaster.propgate.invalid. (
                1 7200 3600 1209600 60 )
@       IN NS   ns-divergent.test.

; dns-auth would serve the expected value for this name; this server does not.
_propgate-verify    IN TXT  "propgate-site-verification=STALE-VALUE"

; Present here, absent elsewhere: divergence in the other direction.
only-here           IN TXT  "visible-from-one-vantage-point-only"
